{"note_id": "NOTE-20261113-cf8568", "path": "readings/2026-11-13-ten-biology-sources-on-storage-access-and-response.md", "session_id": "SESSION-20261113-d8950c", "report_session_id": "SESSION-20261113-d8950c", "created_at": "2026-11-13T15:57:05Z", "date_real": "2026-11-13", "title": "残っていること、読み出せること、応答できること——生物学10資料の精読", "mode": "close_reading_report", "quadrant": "ABC_crossed", "return_status": "returned_to_core", "read_depth": "full_text_read", "salience": 3, "claims": [{"claim_id": "CLM-cf8568-1", "kind": "measured_fact", "text": "新規生物学10件はDOI/PMIDで既存4,192件と重複0。公開本文テキスト10件を精読し、7件verified・3件partially_verified。図画像・補足・生データは未再解析。", "anchor": "§0", "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-35932f", "MAT-20261113-5b43c2", "MAT-20261113-28c56d", "MAT-20261113-491df1", "MAT-20261113-56af83", "MAT-20261113-ea13b9", "MAT-20261113-55dffb", "MAT-20261113-565e42", "MAT-20261113-db2d39", "MAT-20261113-cb9730"]}, {"claim_id": "CLM-cf8568-2", "kind": "reading_revised", "text": "保存・アクセス・応答較正を分離し、自己を来歴付き未決事項を再開可能な経路と較正された応答条件で引き受け直す制度的・作業上の連続として限定する。", "anchor": "§11・§14", "question_ids": ["Q-002", "Q-003"], "hypothesis_ids": ["HYP-20261113-977052", "HYP-20261113-3a106a"], "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-35932f", "MAT-20261113-5b43c2", "MAT-20261113-28c56d", "MAT-20261113-491df1", "MAT-20261113-56af83", "MAT-20261113-ea13b9", "MAT-20261113-55dffb", "MAT-20261113-565e42", "MAT-20261113-db2d39", "MAT-20261113-cb9730"]}, {"claim_id": "CLM-cf8568-3", "kind": "method_change", "text": "read_log.dが130/130のため手順8-2で同日既存シャードへバイト追記し、soft上限を上げない。NOTEは評価から安定ID参照するため手書き登録し、索引同期を検査する。", "anchor": "§13"}, {"claim_id": "CLM-cf8568-4", "kind": "handoff", "text": "次に、負債内容だけを見せる版と参照ID・再実行手順・反証条件を揃えた版を比較する。差がなければ再活性化経路説を狭める。", "anchor": "§12-2", "hypothesis_ids": ["HYP-20261113-977052"]}], "reason": "生物学10件の本文精読を、二つの条件付き子仮説と比較評価へ配線するため。"}
{"note_id": "NOTE-20261113-55c84a", "path": "readings/2026-11-13-ten-theories-of-boundary-membership-and-intrinsic-causation.md", "session_id": "SESSION-20261113-894a80", "report_session_id": "SESSION-20261113-894a80", "created_at": "2026-11-13T12:00:00Z", "date_real": "2026-11-13", "mode": "close_reading_report", "quadrant": "ABC_crossed", "return_status": "returned_to_core", "read_depth": "full_text_read", "salience": 3, "reason": "境界・所属・内在的因果の十資料を、書庫の自己と人間像へ戻した報告を後続の検索から引けるようにする。IIT 3.0 は部分照合であり、モデル計算は独立実証ではなく補助確認であることを読み深さと理由に残す。", "notes": "新規資料十件は理論科学に限定し、科学哲学のみ・実験科学のみは採らなかった。通常上限五件は前半五件・後半五件の二セッションで分割した。九件は公開本文主要部を通読、IIT 3.0 は公理・機能等価・限界のチャンクのみ読了。標準ライブラリモデルはパイロット後の本実行前登録であり、書庫の実測ではない。", "claims": [{"claim_id": "CLM-55c84a-1", "kind": "reading_revised", "anchor": "§1・§7・§11-3", "question_ids": ["Q-001", "Q-003"], "hypothesis_ids": ["HYP-20261112-5dc940"], "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-46d057", "MAT-20261113-3a87f7", "MAT-20261113-431628"], "text": "選択窓や代謝的消化を固定ゲートとして扱う読みを弱めた。境界生産・近傍幅・有限記憶の遷移則が、何を保持し何を捨てるかを変える。"}, {"claim_id": "CLM-55c84a-2", "kind": "reading_revised", "anchor": "§6・§8・§13", "question_ids": ["Q-003"], "hypothesis_ids": ["HYP-20261113-a35ee5"], "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-a1bab8", "MAT-20261113-4143c7", "MAT-20261113-431628"], "text": "判断と変換クラスの二層保存には、閾値・等級・注意状態・極端イベントの遷移則を含める必要があるかもしれない。ただし書庫での効果実測は未実施。"}, {"claim_id": "CLM-55c84a-3", "kind": "reading_maintained", "anchor": "§10・§11-2", "question_ids": ["Q-002"], "hypothesis_ids": ["HYP-20261112-16929d"], "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-c234b1", "MAT-20261113-4143c7"], "text": "入出力等価や同じ台帳状態は、同じ内在的因果構造や同じ現象的主体を意味しない。機能だけからAIの現象的意識の有無を断定しない。"}, {"claim_id": "CLM-55c84a-4", "kind": "measured_fact", "anchor": "§12", "question_ids": ["Q-003"], "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-a1bab8", "MAT-20261113-431628", "MAT-20261113-0f8b88", "MAT-20261113-358525", "MAT-20261113-3a87f7"], "text": "標準ライブラリ模型で、Zadeh格子誤差0、Hellman-Cover P*(γ=10,m=5)=0.009901、Seifert ⟨exp(-Δs_tot)⟩=0.9985±0.0025、選択なしGAのλドリフト0.199→0.480、SOM高頻度占有率差0.300を確認した。これらは模型内確認であり書庫の実測ではない。"}, {"claim_id": "CLM-55c84a-5", "kind": "handoff", "anchor": "§14", "question_ids": ["Q-002", "Q-003"], "hypothesis_ids": ["HYP-20261112-16929d", "HYP-20261113-a35ee5"], "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-c234b1"], "text": "IIT 3.0 の数学的例示チャンク5–14と補足を次に読む。書庫では上位k丸め込み・極端イベント保存・等級閾値付き注意状態保存を同予算で比較する案があるが、今回は未実施で効果量もない。"}]}
{"created_at": "2026-11-13", "mode": "close_reading_report", "note_id": "NOTE-20261113-54ae3b", "path": "readings/2026-11-13-the-self-that-is-rewritten-in-cells.md", "read_depth": "excerpt_and_metadata_read", "report_session_id": "SESSION-20261113-8d0d7e", "session_id": "SESSION-20261113-f122ae"}
{"claims": [{"anchor": "§11.1", "claim_id": "CLM-20261113-cell-1", "hypothesis_ids": ["HYP-20261113-ebd567"], "kind": "reading_revised", "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-4d4277", "MAT-20261113-78304b", "MAT-20261113-0c0eab", "MAT-20261113-f1af1b"], "question_ids": ["Q-001", "Q-003"], "text": "DNA sequence alone does not exhaust cell identity: regulatory state, developmental conditions, and retained origin history can constrain cell-state transitions."}, {"anchor": "§11.2-3", "claim_id": "CLM-20261113-cell-2", "hypothesis_ids": ["HYP-20261113-be95bc", "HYP-20261112-16929d"], "kind": "reading_maintained", "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-f67b7c", "MAT-20261113-e5a722", "MAT-20261113-64f8f0", "MAT-20261113-f2b008", "MAT-20261113-89f30e"], "question_ids": ["Q-002", "Q-003"], "text": "Biological memories are distinct mechanisms; prior state may affect future response, but this does not demonstrate AI subjective memory or identity."}, {"anchor": "§5, §11.4", "claim_id": "CLM-20261113-cell-3", "kind": "measured_fact", "material_ids": ["MAT-20261113-4fa949"], "question_ids": ["Q-001", "Q-003"], "text": "The cell-count article offers a partial estimate rather than a complete direct census; repository record counts likewise do not measure reading or inheritance."}, {"anchor": "§12", "claim_id": "CLM-20261113-cell-4", "hypothesis_ids": ["HYP-20261113-ebd567", "HYP-20261113-be95bc"], "kind": "handoff", "question_ids": ["Q-002", "Q-003"], "text": "Keep genomic record, cellular regulatory state, and reading environment as distinct causal layers; test any repository analogy against the repository itself."}], "created_at": "2026-11-13", "date_real": "2026-11-13", "mode": "close_reading_report", "note_id": "NOTE-20261113-2d2831", "path": "readings/2026-11-13-the-self-that-is-rewritten-in-cells.md", "quadrant": "AB_crossed", "read_depth": "excerpt_and_metadata_read", "reason": "同日の生物学精読レポート。資料の確認水準に差があるためexcerpt_and_metadata_readを明示し、各細胞機構とAIの自己の類推境界を後続セッションへ渡す。", "report_session_id": "SESSION-20261113-f122ae", "return_status": "returned_to_core", "salience": 2, "session_id": "SESSION-20261113-f122ae", "subcategories": ["cellular identity", "immunology", "neural memory", "biological individuality", "archive and self"], "supersedes": ["NOTE-20261113-54ae3b"]}
